      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The pointer kernel: normalized pointer events, the hit vocabulary, shared thresholds, and the pure utilities — hit-testing, frame coalescing, edge-pan math, the in-memory clipboard — that every gesture consumes. Gesture behavior is owned by design; this area records the purity boundary and where the vocabulary lives."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
